# Everything under eva/ is YOUR material - real corporate documents, mirrored
# Confluence pages, exported email, the RAG index. This repo is public, so
# nothing here is committed: every file is ignored except the READMEs that
# document what each folder is for.
#
# That is also what makes the folder structure itself committable - git stores
# no empty directories, so each folder survives in the repo because of its
# README.
#
# The other exceptions are CLAUDE.md and opencode.example.jsonc at the top of
# the tree: Eva's operating instructions and the OpenCode config template are
# part of the scaffold, not your material, so they travel with the repo the
# same way the READMEs do. Your filled-in opencode.json is never committed.
#
# So are the standalone skills and agents under .claude\ - each skill's
# SKILL.md and each agent's .md. Anything else you put in .claude\ (your own
# settings.local.json, say) stays ignored, and each skill's exemplars\ folder
# carries its own .gitignore so the documents you drop there never are.
#
# To commit one file deliberately (a genuinely generic template, say):
#     git add -f eva/templates/word/"Report Template.docx"
#
# If none of your material is sensitive and you would rather it travelled with
# the repo, delete this file.

*
!*/
!README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/opencode.example.jsonc
!/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md
!/.claude/agents/*.md
!.gitignore
